{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"GnustoSpellcasting"}],"title":"GnustoSpellcasting","externalID":"GnustoSpellcasting","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four ways a spell becomes available, over one way of writing what it does."}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"The-bundle","title":"The bundle","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/init(memorySlots:maxMana:)","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/memorySlots","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/maxMana"]},{"anchor":"Registering-a-spell","title":"Registering a spell","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/spell(_:cost:effect:)"]},{"anchor":"The-four-paradigms","title":"The four paradigms","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/cantrip","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/energy(_:)","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/scroll(_:)"]},{"anchor":"What-the-bundle-contributes-to-the-host","title":"What the bundle contributes to the host","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/verbs","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/actions","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/noiseWords"]},{"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Gnusto"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Magic systems differ in their bookkeeping, not in their effects. An at-will"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cantrip, a spell memorized from a book and spent in the speaking, a bolt paid"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for out of an energy pool, and a scroll good for one reading all do the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sort of thing to the world; what separates them is when the game says no. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library keeps the two apart. A spell’s effect is an ordinary rule body, written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly as any other rule body is, and a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" sits beside it deciding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"availability and price."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A spell’s identity is its own intent, declared with "},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" like any custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verb, so "},{"code":"glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"cast glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"read passwall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are parser rows and a spell can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carry as many phrasings as its author wants. "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/spell(_:cost:effect:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns the actions that intent needs — the cast handler, plus the memorize"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler when the cost is "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — and the game"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splices them into its "},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is a "},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle rather than a "},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", because it has state to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"save. The finite spell memory and the energy pool are "},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s it owns, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"both travel in a save and come back correctly under UNDO; the defaults are 3"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slots and 12 mana. Everything else is the host’s: the spellbook, the scroll, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets, and every word of prose an effect prints. The bundle contributes two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verbs of its own — "},{"code":"rest","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"code":"meditate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), which refills the pool, and "},{"code":"spells","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(or "},{"code":"magic","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), which reports what is held in mind and how much energy is left —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and adds "},{"code":"spell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to the parser’s noise words, so "},{"code":"cast the glow spell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reaches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Casting runs gate, effect, pay. Availability is checked first; the effect runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second and may refuse on its own account with "},{"code":"require","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"reply","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; only an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effect that finished pays. So a firebolt aimed at nothing costs no energy, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scroll read at the wrong wall survives."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Wiring it in","anchor":"Wiring-it-in"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Gnusto","import GnustoSpellcasting","","extension Intent {","    #verb(\"glow\", [\"glow\"], [\"cast\", \"glow\"])","    #verb(","        \"firebolt\", [\"firebolt\"], [\"cast\", \"firebolt\"],","        [\"firebolt\", .directObject], [\"cast\", \"firebolt\", \"at\", .directObject])","}","","struct Tower: Game {","    let magic = Spellcasting(memorySlots: 3, maxMana: 12)","","    var content: GameContents { magic }","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { [.glow, .firebolt] }","","    var actions: [IntentAction] {","        magic.spell(.glow, cost: .cantrip) {","            say(\"Pale light seeps from your fingers.\")","        }","        magic.spell(.firebolt, cost: .energy(4)) {","            guard let target = command.directObject else {","                try reply(\"Cast firebolt at what?\")","            }","            target.vanish()","            say(\"Fire leaps from your hand and bursts against \\(target.definiteName).\")","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" spell carries its own memorize intent,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the one "},{"code":"spell(_:cost:effect:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call registers both halves:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["magic.spell(.unbar, cost: .prepared(book: spellbook, learnVia: .learnUnbar)) {","    try require(!wardedDoor.isOpen, else: \"The door already stands open.\")","    wardedDoor.isOpen = true","    say(\"The warding-marks gutter and die, and the door drifts open.\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass "},{"code":"book: nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the spell can be memorized anywhere; pass an item and it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has to be in hand."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The worked example","anchor":"The-worked-example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/Gramarye\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a small original game built to test the claim in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first sentence of this page. It runs one spell per paradigm and chains them so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each opens exactly one obstacle: the cantrip finds the scroll, the memorized"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spell opens the warded door, the energy spell destroys the golem, the scroll"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes the wall. Remove any one of the four and the amulet is unreachable, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a stronger demonstration than four spells that happen to work. Its design"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document is "},{"code":"docs\/games\/gramarye.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"references":{"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/Spellcasting/spell(_:cost:effect:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcasting\/spell(_:cost:effect:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/spell(_:cost:effect:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"spell","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Intent","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto6IntentV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cost","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpellCost","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:18GnustoSpellcasting9SpellCostO"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"effect","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"text":") -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"IntentAction","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto12IntentActionV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"spell(_:cost:effect:)","abstract":[{"text":"Registers one spell: the stage-4 behavior that casting its ","type":"text"},{"code":"intent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"performs, and — for a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" spell — the behavior","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of memorizing it via ","type":"text"},{"code":"prepareIntent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Splice the result into the game’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/Spellcasting":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Spellcasting"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Spellcasting"}],"title":"Spellcasting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A reusable spellcasting layer covering the common RPG magic paradigms —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at-will cantrips, memorized (“Vancian”) spells, an energy\/points pool, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one-shot scrolls — over a single, uniform notion of a spell."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcasting"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting","kind":"symbol","title":"GnustoSpellcasting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Four ways a spell becomes available, over one way of writing what it does."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/SpellCost":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcost","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SpellCost","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpellCost","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SpellCost","abstract":[{"text":"How a spell becomes available to cast, and what casting it costs — the axis","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that lets one spellcasting system express the common RPG magic paradigms","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without changing how a spell’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"effect"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is written.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/SpellCost/scroll(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcost\/scroll(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/scroll(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scroll","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"SpellCost.scroll(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Read from the given scroll item, which is consumed when the spell is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cast. Refused unless the scroll is in hand.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/Spellcasting/noiseWords":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcasting\/noisewords","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/noiseWords","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"noiseWords"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"title":"noiseWords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"“spell” is filler in a casting game — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cast the glow spell"},{"type":"text","text":" should"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parse as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cast glow"},{"type":"text","text":" — so the layer adds it to the parser’s noise set."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoSpellcasting/documentation/GnustoSpellcasting/Spellcasting/init(memorySlots:maxMana:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnustospellcasting\/spellcasting\/init(memoryslots:maxmana:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellc